From d6b86595c0d5c5474e89afaeb6a07f3527f86c8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:16:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat(telemetry): report real host metrics, or null, never
 fabricated values

Live mode presented several invented figures as measurements:

- watts was literally node_count * 220.
- trustScore was a hardcoded 85 that no collector ever wrote.
- totalIops/ingressMbps/egressMbps were read from a state file only the
  dashboards endpoint populated, so polling /telemetry/environment alone
  returned a permanent 0.
- cpuPercent/ramPercent returned 0.0 when metrics-server was absent,
  indistinguishable from a genuinely idle cluster.
- clusterReady matched the pod names rke2-server/rke2-ingress-nginx, so it
  never became true on K3s even though the installer supports both.

Add host_metrics.py reading real kernel counters: power from Intel RAPL or
IPMI DCMI, IOPS from /proc/diskstats, throughput from /proc/net/dev, with
virtual devices excluded and rates differenced across samples. Derive
openCves/trustScore from Trivy VulnerabilityReports. Base readiness on node
Ready conditions, which are distribution-agnostic.

Unavailable sources now return null with a reason in metricSources instead
of a plausible-looking number. Also guard _save_state, which raised
PermissionError and 503'd the whole endpoint when /var/lib/nexus was not
writable.

Verified against a live k3s cluster: cpuPercent 5.5 / ramPercent 17.5 match
'kubectl top nodes' (5% / 17%); totalIops tracked a 400 MB write at 8074
IOPS; watts stayed null on a VM with no RAPL or BMC.
